      { "id": "dc-sec-conn", "kind": "section", "label": "Holding the sockets open", "x": 12, "y": 44, "width": 760, "height": 120, "tone": 0 },
      { "id": "dc-sec-msg", "kind": "section", "label": "Writing a message", "x": 12, "y": 304, "width": 760, "height": 120, "tone": 1 },
      { "id": "dc-sec-push", "kind": "section", "label": "Pushing it out", "x": 1052, "y": 44, "width": 240, "height": 380, "tone": 2 },
      { "id": "dc-sec-search", "kind": "section", "label": "Indexed later, off to the side", "x": 792, "y": 498, "width": 760, "height": 120, "tone": 3 },
      { "id": "dc-sec-media", "kind": "section", "label": "Attachments", "x": 12, "y": 628, "width": 760, "height": 120, "tone": 4 },
      { "id": "dc-sec-voice", "kind": "section", "label": "Voice, on its own hardware", "x": 12, "y": 822, "width": 760, "height": 250, "tone": 5 },
      {
        "id": "dc-note-conn", "kind": "note",
        "text": "The gateway counts open connections, not requests. 30 new a second, each held for 40 seconds, is 1200 sockets against a ceiling of 1600. Double the load and it starts refusing connections outright.",
        "x": 1320, "y": 48, "width": 300, "size": "md", "font": "hand"
      },
      {
        "id": "dc-note-fanout", "kind": "note",
        "text": "Drag the message rate up and watch the push servers. One message becomes one delivery per pod, and each pod can only do about 130 a second. Past that, members stop seeing messages while the senders see no errors at all. That silence is what makes fan-out hard.",
        "x": 1608, "y": 272, "width": 320, "size": "md", "font": "hand"
      },
      {
        "id": "dc-note-hot", "kind": "note",
        "text": "Messages are split across six channel shards. Give the message store a hot key and one busy channel takes far more than its share, so that shard melts while the average still looks healthy.",
        "x": 792, "y": 760, "width": 300, "size": "md", "font": "hand"
      },
      {
        "id": "dc-note-voice", "kind": "note",
        "text": "Voice runs on its own servers and never touches the text path, so chat can be on fire while calls stay up.",
        "x": 792, "y": 976, "width": 300, "size": "md", "font": "hand"
      }
    ]
  }
